                <pb facs="0844" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg758"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July 31,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Leishman reports that after exhausting every ordinary means to force the
                    Sublime Porte to conclude the promised settling of the school and other matters
                    he feels compelled to ask the Department of State for further instructions, as
                    it appears useless for him to attempt to prosecute matters further on present
                    lines, and unless some more forcible measure be adopted he fears the promised
                    settlement of the school question will drag on indefinitely.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
